bg=#fff5de</panel_attributes><additional_attributes></additional_attributes></element><element><id>UMLNote</id><coordinates><x>0</x><y>3078</y><w>1944</w><h>153</h></coordinates><panel_attributes>Reading notes
Class boxes show selected members, including cross-package reference types.
InventorHub is an alias, not a subclass. IMU is not a Sensor subclass.
Model and DriveBase both register with the clock; registration is based on callable step().
Steppable is a type-checking protocol, not a runtime requirement.
The active world is read dynamically. Mounts store SensorModel objects.
Includes the example BumperContact adapter. Tests are outside this diagram.
bg=#f4f6f8</panel_attributes><additional_attributes></additional_attributes></element><element><id>UMLNote</id><coordinates><x>1458</x><y>1341</y><w>486</w><h>117</h></coordinates><panel_attributes>Clock phases
0: motors, sensors, hub
1: drive body
1.5: IMU integration
2: DriveBase control / contact adapter
